// everyday path. emit-x86 is a side printer. Did not run shell. Did not edit
// the product tree.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Quote x86_empty.oo on disk and the no-main lock in x86_emit_walk.oo.
//   2. Score the missing x86_nomain.oo: what body must PV1 add.
//   3. Score the silent-_start attack: x86_emit_sys.oo always writes _start.
//   4. State [x] / [ ] status. Stop.
//
// residual: did not run the smokes. oodac/oodac was not rebuilt. did not
// copy any overlay. did not touch c_emit*, llvm*, wasm*, cli, guide.

## 0. Verdict

  [x] x86_empty.oo exists at ooda/fixtures/x86_empty.oo. Its body is a
      comment only. The harvest walk must ERR before x86_emit_linux64
      gets an empty list.
  [x] x86_emit_walk.oo:201-204 catches `!saw_main` with
      `ERR\tx86_emit\tresidual: need fn main` and `process_exit(1)`.
  [x] x86_emit_walk.oo:209-212 catches an empty msgs list with
      `ERR\tx86_emit\tresidual: need println(\"...\") (not emit-c)` and
      `process_exit(1)`. This blocks the silent-_start path that
      x86_emit_sys.oo:36-67 would otherwise write.
  [ ] x86_nomain.oo is MISSING from ooda/fixtures/. PV1 has not yet
      written it. The phalanx plan names this fixture but the role has
      not landed it.

  The two existing ERR gates cover the hostile shape that x86_empty.oo
  was written to test. The second fixture (x86_nomain.oo) is a parallel
  attack with a different body: a non-main `fn` so `saw_main` stays
  false on a source that does have a function.

