## 2. x86_empty.oo on disk

  File: ooda/fixtures/x86_empty.oo. 12 lines. Header is the four-element
  Academy shape (Title, Logline, Setup, Beats). Body is `// no items`.

  Header (exact):

    // # Empty of functions
    //
    // Logline: Comment only so emit-x86 must fail closed.
    //
    // Setup: No fn. No println.
    //
    // Beats:
    //   1. Leave no function.
    //   2. Leave no println.
    //   3. Force emit-x86 to print ERR.

  Beat 3 names the contract: `emit-x86` must print `ERR`.

  Token walk for this body:
    - `chars_len(src) > 0`. x86_emit.oo:26-29 does not fire.
    - `x86_fold_hello(src)` returns `""`. x86_emit_fold.oo:177-191
      needs the greet shape. No fn greet. Empty return.
    - All four call matchers (id, snd, cat, greet) miss. x86_emit.oo:39-58.
    - `x86_collect_prints(toks)` runs (x86_emit_walk.oo:13). The walk
      sees no KW_FN, so `saw_main` stays false. Lines 201-204 fire:
        println("ERR\tx86_emit\tresidual: need fn main");
        process_exit(1);
    - Exit 1. No .s written. No _start. No silent ELF.

  Status: [x]. The fixture is on disk and the lock matches its beat 3.

