  What PV1 must add (does not add in this wave, the wave is spec-only):

    // # emit-x86 non-main fn only
    //
    // Logline: A non-main fn so emit-x86 must ERR saw_main=false
    //          even though the source has a function.
    //
    // Setup: fn helper() with no body println. No fn main.
    //
    // Beats:
    //   1. Declare fn helper.
    //   2. Leave no fn main.
    //   3. Force emit-x86 to print ERR need fn main.

  Token walk for that body:
    - KW_FN at the helper. x86_emit_walk.oo:31-46 fires. IDENT text is
      `helper`, not `main`. `saw_main` stays false.
    - No println. `leftover_unresolved` stays false.
    - Line 201-204: `!saw_main` → `ERR\tx86_emit\tresidual: need fn
      main` → `process_exit(1)`.
    - Same ERR string as x86_empty.oo. Two fixtures, two shapes, one
